    "<p>Fix the common fence height <code>h</code>. Every original plank of height <code>h</code> can be used by itself.</p>",
    "<p>Any remaining plank of height <code>x &lt; h</code> can only be used by pairing it with a plank of height <code>h - x</code>.</p>",
    "<p>Using the frequency of each height, count these disjoint pairs with <code>min(freq[x], freq[h - x])</code>; when <code>x == h - x</code>, use <code>freq[x] / 2</code>.</p>",
    "<p>It is enough to try heights that occur as an original plank height or as the sum of two original plank heights. Take the maximum number of single planks and pairs over all such heights.</p>"
